        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done — pyknotid 0.5.3 is built from source, installed into the system Python (editable install at `/app/pyknotid`), and works with NumPy 2.3.0.\n\n**What was done:**\n1. Cloned the repo to `/app/pyknotid` (branch 0.5.3).\n2. Installed `setuptools`, `wheel`, `cython`, then compiled all four Cython extensions (`chelpers`, `ccomplexity`, `coctree`, `cinvariants`) via `python setup.py build_ext --inplace` against NumPy 2.3 headers.\n3. `pip install -e .` for the global environment.\n\n**NumPy/Python-3.13 compatibility fixes:**\n- `pyknotid/make/torus.py`: `from fractions import gcd` → `from math import gcd`.\n- Removed removed NumPy aliases across `spacecurve.py`, `periodiccell.py`, `periodic_knot.py`, `invariants.py`, `dtnotation.py`, `openknot.py`, `knot.py`, `representation.py`: `np.float/n.int/np.bool/n.complex` → builtin `float/int/bool/complex`.\n- `pyknotid/representations/representation.py`: adapted to the current `planarity` API, which now returns node attrs `vertex_position/vertex_start/vertex_end` and edge attrs `edge_position/edge_start/edge_end` instead of the old `pos/start/end`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- README snippet runs cleanly; `alexander_polynomial(-1)` of a three-twist knot returns ≈ 7 as expected.\n- All Cython `.so` modules import from their original package locations.\n- Test suite: **18 passed** (`tests/test_random_curves.py` and `tests/test_catalogue.py` excluded as instructed).",
            "session_id": "tb-17ce2354be"
        }
